content.text:
Now add `openTutorial` method. Place after openDialogue or before. It should render story/tutorial with steps. Mark settings.tutorialSeen true and save when auto. Include close/start button. Use t. Also perhaps if opened from settings, don't mark? Mark anyway.

Implementation:
```js
openTutorial(auto=false){
  this.settings.tutorialSeen=true; this.save();
  const steps=[...];
  this.openModal({
    title:t('tutorial.title'), subtitle:t('tutorial.subtitle'), icon:'✦', wide:true,
    body:`<div class="tutorial-hero">...`,
    footer:`<span>${t('tutorial.reopen')}</span><button class="btn primary small" id="tutorialStart">${t('tutorial.start')}</button>`,
    onMount:(root)=>{ root.querySelector('#tutorialStart').onclick=()=>this.closeModal(); }
  });
}
```
Need CSS for tutorial. We'll add.

Use `.tutorial-grid`, `.tutorial-step`, `.tutorial-story`.

Let's add method before chat helpers.

